    13	   Let Ce 2 and C2 be two copies of the complex plane, and let f : C      e 2 → C2 be
    14	a locally invertible polynomial mapping, i.e. f (x1 , x2 ) = (f1 (x1 , x2 ), f2 (x1 , x2 )),
    15	where f1 and f2 are polynomials in x1 and x2 with complex coefficients such that
    16	
