    57	   We hope that some of our results may appear to be of some use in proving the
    58	Jacobian Conjecture. Since a lot of wrong proofs of the Jacobian Conjecture have
    59	appeared (see [2], Sect. I.3), we shall try, as far as possible, for all our assertions,
    60	either to provide proofs in maximal (sometimes, maybe, excessive) detail or to refer
    61	to such proofs. In particular, we prove some statements which were used by others
    62	but whose proofs were omitted or sketched because of their evidence.
